  "_comment": "Regions are [x, y, w, h] in window pixels at the 1024x768 table resolution (960x666 game area). Wine windows carry a 19 px Wine-drawn menu bar on top; the native window has none but draws a small ImGui 'Menu' strip over the top ~20 px, so 'table' skips those rows on both sides. Native Dragon/Pirates regions are Wine's shifted by (+1, -19) as measured for Space Cadet (not measured separately for those tables). 'upper'/'lower' split the playfield at the 1 px seam measured near native y 330 (Wine upper half = native +19 rows, lower half = native +18). '_displays' = [first, last] Xvfb display numbers the harness may use (inclusive: :90-:139). '*-audio' targets: wine-*-audio run in the private audio prefix (FT_WINEPREFIX_AUDIO, required, no default: a private copy made by harness.py init-audio-prefix and deleted by whoever made it) with Wine's alsa driver and ALSA_CONFIG_PATH=re/test/audio/asound_null.conf (pcm.!default = null), so DirectSound exists and nothing reaches a real device (measured: DRAGON NewGame sound entry is non-zero with audio, see README Audio); native-*-audio drop -noaudio, set SDL_AUDIODRIVER=dummy and Sounds=1, Music=1. 'audio_probe' = exe globals for scripts/audio_probe.py (DirectSound pointer, sound_list base and count, the table object pointer global and the offset of NewGame's SoundIndex1 in it).",
